          ]
        },
        {
          "type": "paragraph",
          "spans": [
            {
              "text": "Read the map from the right: cycle time is mostly waiting, and every lever the book offers acts on waiting through work in progress or utilization.",
              "cites": [
                "ch01/s01/p002",
                "ch07/s01/p001"
              ]
            }
          ]
        }
      ]
    },
    {
      "key": "deep_dive",
      "title": "The core ideas in depth",
      "blocks": [
        {
          "type": "heading",
          "level": 2,
          "text": "Little's law"
        },
        {
          "type": "definition",
          "term": "Little's law",
          "spans": [
            {
              "text": "Average work in progress equals throughput times average time in the system.",
              "cites": [
                "ch02/s01/p001"
              ]
            }
          ]
        },
        {
          "type": "paragraph",
          "spans": [
            {
              "text": "Because throughput is set by capacity, adding work in progress without adding capacity only lengthens the time each item spends inside; ",
              "cites": [
                "ch02/s01/p003",
                "ch02/s01/p005"
              ]
            },
            {
              "text": "the same identity turns into a forecast: divide the items in progress by weekly throughput to get the expected wait.",
              "cites": [
                "ch02/s02/p002"
              ]
            }
          ]
        },
        {
          "type": "callout",
          "tone": "antipattern",
          "spans": [
            {
              "text": "Starting more work to speed up delivery: at fixed throughput it can only make every item later.",
              "cites": [
                "ch02/s01/p005"
              ]
            }
          ]
        },
        {
          "type": "heading",
          "level": 2,
          "text": "The utilization curve"
        },
        {
          "type": "paragraph",
          "spans": [
            {
              "text": "Waiting stays modest up to about 70% utilization and then rises steeply: at 90% an item waits about nine times its service time.",
              "cites": [
                "ch03/s01/p004",
                "ch03/s01/f001"
              ]
            }
          ]
        },
        {
          "type": "chart",
          "kind": "line",
          "title": "Waiting time against utilization",
          "x": {
            "label": "Utilization (%)",
            "values": [
              50,
              70,
              80,
              90,
              95
            ]
          },
          "y": {
            "label": "Wait (× service time)"
          },
          "series": [
            {
              "name": "Wait",
              "values": [
                1,
                2.3,
                4,
                9,
                19
              ]
            }
          ],
          "cites": [
            "ch03/s01/f001"
          ]
        },
        {
          "type": "callout",
          "tone": "insight",
          "spans": [
            {
              "text": "Variability multiplies the effect of utilization, which is why the same load feels fine one week and jammed the next.",
              "cites": [
                "ch03/s02/p003",
                "ch03/s02/p006"
              ]
            }
          ]
        },
        {
          "type": "callout",
          "tone": "remember",
          "spans": [
            {
              "text": "Keep 15–20% of capacity unallocated.",
              "cites": [
                "ch03/s03/p006"
              ]
            }
          ]
        },
        {
          "type": "heading",
          "level": 2,
          "text": "Limiting work in progress"
        },
        {
          "type": "steps",
          "items": [
            [
              {
                "text": "Count the items in progress per person today.",
                "cites": [
                  "ch04/s01/p001"
                ]
              }
            ],
            [
              {
                "text": "Set the limit just below that count and make it visible on the board.",
                "cites": [
                  "ch04/s01/p002"
                ]
              }
            ],
            [
              {
                "text": "When the limit is reached, help finish an item instead of starting one.",
                "cites": [
                  "ch04/s01/p003"
                ]
              }
            ]
          ]
        },
        {
          "type": "table",
          "header": [
            "Measure",
            "Before limits",
            "After limits"
          ],
          "rows": [
            [
              {
                "text": "Average cycle time",
                "cites": [
                  "ch04/s02/t001"
                ]
              },
              {
                "text": "31 days",
                "cites": [
                  "ch04/s02/t001"
                ]
              },
              {
                "text": "about 10 days",
                "cites": [
                  "ch04/s02/t001"
                ]
              }
            ],
            [
              {
                "text": "Throughput",
                "cites": [
                  "ch04/s02/t001"
                ]
              },
              {
                "text": "flat",
                "cites": [
                  "ch04/s02/p005"
                ]
              },
              {
                "text": "flat",
                "cites": [
                  "ch04/s02/p005"
                ]
              }
            ]
          ]
        },
        {
          "type": "callout",
          "tone": "caution",
          "spans": [
            {
              "text": "The evidence comes from teams the author worked with over twelve weeks.",
              "cites": [
                "ch04/s02/p001"
              ]
            }
          ]
        },
        {
          "type": "heading",
          "level": 2,
          "text": "Hidden queues"
        },
        {
          "type": "paragraph",
          "spans": [
            {
              "text": "Most waiting happens where nobody measures it — approvals, hand-offs and work turned away at a limit — so it has to be made visible before it can be managed.",
              "cites": [
                "ch06/s01/p001",
                "ch06/s02/p004",
                "ch04/s03/p003"
              ]
            }
          ]
        }
      ]
    },
    {
      "key": "practice",
      "title": "Putting the book to work",
      "blocks": [
        {
          "type": "steps",
          "items": [
            [
              {
                "text": "Map every queue an item passes through, including approvals and hand-offs.",
                "cites": [
                  "ch06/s02/p004"
                ]
              }
            ],
            [
              {
                "text": "Measure throughput per week and forecast from WIP divided by throughput.",
                "cites": [
                  "ch02/s02/p002"
                ]
              }
            ],
            [
              {
                "text": "Set an explicit WIP limit and stop starting before you start finishing.",
                "cites": [
                  "ch04/s01/p002"
                ]
              }
            ],
            [
              {
                "text": "Plan with 15–20% of capacity unallocated.",
                "cites": [
                  "ch03/s03/p006"
                ]
              }
            ],
            [
              {
                "text": "Cut batch sizes so less work sits in the system at once.",
                "cites": [
                  "ch05/s02/p003"
                ]
              }
            ],
            [
              {
                "text": "Review utilization weekly and cut intake once it passes 80%.",
                "cites": [
                  "ch03/s03/p007"
                ]
              }
            ]
          ]
        },
        {
          "type": "callout",
          "tone": "antipattern",
          "spans": [
            {
              "text": "Responding to slow delivery by starting more work, or by planning people to 100% of their time.",
              "cites": [
                "ch02/s01/p005",
                "ch03/s03/p002"
              ]
            }
          ]
        }
      ]
    }
  ],
  "journey": [
    {
      "anchor": "ch01",
      "role": "setup",
      "takeaway": [
        {
          "text": "Establishes that delivery time is mostly waiting time — the fact the rest of the book explains.",
          "cites": [
            "ch01/s01/p002"
          ]
        }
      ]
    },
    {
      "anchor": "ch02",
      "role": "concept",
      "takeaway": [
        {
          "text": "Supplies the first mechanism: at fixed throughput, more work in progress means longer waits.",
          "cites": [
            "ch02/s01/p001"
          ]
        }
      ]
    },
    {
      "anchor": "ch03",
      "role": "concept",
      "takeaway": [
        {
          "text": "Adds the second: past about 80% utilization, waiting explodes, and variability makes it worse.",
          "cites": [
            "ch03/s01/p004",
            "ch03/s02/p003"
          ]
        }
      ]
    },
    {
      "anchor": "ch04",
      "role": "evidence",
      "takeaway": [
        {
          "text": "Shows WIP limits cutting cycle time from 31 to about 10 days with flat throughput.",
          "cites": [
            "ch04/s02/t001"
          ]
        }
      ]
    },
    {
      "anchor": "ch05",
      "role": "method",
      "takeaway": [
        {
          "text": "Turns the same arithmetic into a second lever: smaller batches.",
          "cites": [
            "ch05/s02/p003"
          ]
        }
      ]
    },
    {
      "anchor": "ch06",
      "role": "application",
      "takeaway": [
        {
          "text": "Applies the model to the queues nobody measures — approvals and hand-offs.",
          "cites": [
            "ch06/s01/p001"
          ]
        }
      ]
    },
    {
      "anchor": "ch07",
      "role": "synthesis",
      "takeaway": [
        {
          "text": "Recasts management as tending the flow of work, not the busyness of people.",
          "cites": [
            "ch07/s01/p001"
          ]
        }
      ]
    }
  ],
  "themes": [
    {
      "name": "Waiting, not working",
      "spans": [
        {
          "text": "Delivery time is dominated by waiting, first measured in the opening chapter ",
          "cites": [
            "ch01/s01/p002"
          ]
        },
        {
          "text": "and later traced to approvals and hand-offs nobody measures.",
          "cites": [
            "ch06/s01/p001"
          ]
        }
      ]
    },
    {
      "name": "Less in progress, more done",
      "spans": [
        {
          "text": "Little's law makes work in progress the lever, ",
          "cites": [
            "ch02/s01/p001"
          ]
        },
        {
          "text": "WIP limits prove it on real teams, ",
          "cites": [
            "ch04/s02/t001"
          ]
        },
        {
          "text": "and small batches work for the same reason.",
          "cites": [
            "ch05/s02/p003"
          ]
        }
      ]
    },
    {
      "name": "Slack is capacity",
      "spans": [
        {
          "text": "Running people near full utilization guarantees queues; ",
          "cites": [
            "ch03/s01/p004",
            "ch03/s03/p002"
          ]
        },
        {
          "text": "managing flow means protecting slack deliberately.",
          "cites": [
            "ch07/s01/p003"
          ]
        }
      ]
    }
  ],
